Details of Out-of-Domain Evaluation Metrics. To detect reward hacking and verify general visual fidelity, we report seven unseen metrics on DrawBench:
1) Aesthetic Score ( Schuhmann et al., 2022 ) , a CLIP-based linear estimator trained on LAION aesthetic ratings;
2) DeQA ( You et al., 2025 ) , a multimodal LLM assessor sensitive to low-level distortions, blurriness, and synthesis artifacts;
3) CLIPScore ( Hessel et al., 2021 ) , measuring semantic cosine similarity between prompt and image embeddings;
4) HPSv2.1 ( Wu et al., 2023 ) , a fine-tuned human preference model for stylistic and compositional alignment;
5) ImageReward ( Xu et al., 2023 ) ( ImgRwd ), evaluating text–image coherence, structural fidelity, and harmlessness;
6) PickScore ( Kirstain et al., 2023 ) on unseen DrawBench prompts (testing out-of-domain preference for GenEval/OCR models and unseen-prompt generalization for PickScore models); and
7) UnifiedReward ( Wang et al., 2025c ) ( UniRwd ), a unified multimodal human-preference reward model.

